   509	### B.6 21-of-22 census, mismatch energy, iteration, cofinality
   510	
   511	The 21-of-22 off-axis violation frequency is a construction effect
   512	(\(q>\alpha\) or off-axis \(q=\alpha\)), as already computed in
   513	`sol-tdbound-review.md:211-257`. It is not evidence of a conservation
   514	law. Sol is right to demote it.
   515	
   516	Mismatch-energy identity (10.1): from \(C^2=D^2=0\) and \(C\cdot D=td\)
   517	on a common resolution of the two pencils,
   518	\(\sum(R_p/\alpha-S_p/\beta)^2=2\,td/(\alpha\beta)\). Algebraically
   519	correct; no Keller hypothesis beyond generic finiteness. Combined
   520	with Prop 5.8 this is (10.2). KME-2 is exactly TD-BOUND in those
   521	coordinates, not a strictly weaker lemma. Calling KME-2 “the missing
   522	lemma” would be a false reduction: it restates the prize. Sol says
   523	this (“not an independent mechanism lemma”). Keep it diagnostic.
   524	
   525	PCC: \(h_p=\min(\lfloor R_p/\alpha\rfloor,\lfloor S_p/\beta\rfloor)\)
   526	satisfies \(R_p S_p\ge\alpha\beta h_p^2\) because
   527	\(R_p\ge h_p\alpha\) and \(S_p\ge h_p\beta\). Summing and using
   528	\(I_\infty=\sum RS=B^2\alpha\beta-td\) gives \(td\le\alpha\beta\) once
   529	\(\sum h_p^2\ge B^2-1\). So PCC is a genuine *sufficient* lemma. It
   530	is unproved. The needed weighted/Laurent-to-projective transport,
   531	proximity accounting, distinct-center coverage, and no-double-counting
   532	theorem are correctly listed as absent. Hardness 8.5/10 is a
   533	judgment; the statement is precise.
   534	
   535	Iteration (Prop 4): \(td(F^k)=d^k\) for a nonautomorphic Keller map
   536	with \(td(F)=d>1\) is the tower formula for
   537	\([K:(F^k)^*K]\). A universal absolute bound \(td\le N\) for *every*
   538	plane Keller counterexample is therefore equivalent to JC2, not an
   539	intermediate rung. The published \(td\ge 6\) (`REDUCTION.md:340-351`)
   540	makes the premise \(d>1\) automatic here. This does **not** obstruct
   541	a bound on a selected globally minimal counterexample. Sol’s
   542	quantifier correction is mandatory. G5 as actually posed is
   543	type-relative TD-BOUND \(td\le\alpha\beta\), which is compatible with
   544	iteration (the type of \(F^k\) may grow). The iteration paragraph is
   545	a correction of principle for a *universal* bound, not a proof that
   546	TD-BOUND is equivalent to JC2.
   547	
   548	Cofinality: `TDBOUND.md:97-103` claims that TD-BOUND plus “finiteness
   549	of the GGV \((m,n)\)-list” makes the sheet ladder finite.
   550	`REDUCTION.md:225-267` already records that GGV Algorithm 8 is finite
   551	only after an explicit input bound, and that an exhaustive finite GGV
   552	catalog is **NOT ESTABLISHED**. Sol’s CONJECTURE SC is the missing
   553	type cap for a *selected* pair. The cofinality sentence in TDBOUND.md
   554	is not a theorem. Correction accepted.
   555	
   556	### B.7 The missing lemma, stated precisely
   557	
   558	Sol names four statements. They are not interchangeable.
   559	
   560	**SP (single-pole cap).** If a one-pole Sigray configuration is
   561	globally realizable by a polynomial Keller pair, then \(ab\le\nu\).
   562	
   563	This is exactly TD-BOUND restricted to one pole, because
   564	\(td=\alpha\beta\,ab/\nu\) there. It is necessary for any
   565	merge/emission proof: a theorem for every configuration cannot omit
   566	the sector with no multi-leaf merge. Prop 3 satisfies the current
   567	local rules and violates SP by an unbounded factor. FC5 cannot prove
   568	SP: after the first chart it has already forgotten the scale
   569	(\((w,M)=(2/3,3)\) constant). Hardness “8/10” is optimistic if read
   570	as “a lemma.” SP is one-pole JC2 in Sigray coordinates. Isolate it
   571	as the smallest *necessary sector test*, not as an available tool.
   572	
   573	**KME-2.** \(\sum_p(R_p/\alpha-S_p/\beta)^2\le 2\) on a common
   574	resolution. Equivalent to TD-BOUND, \(\sum ab/\nu\le 1\), and
   575	\(\Delta^2\ge -2\). Diagnostic coordinate change, not a reduction.
   576	The exceptional lattice does not imply it: multiples of a root have
   577	arbitrarily negative square. Correct.
   578	
   579	**PCC.** \(\sum_p h_p^2\ge B^2-1\) with
   580	\(h_p=\min(\lfloor R_p/\alpha\rfloor,\lfloor S_p/\beta\rfloor)\).
   581	Sufficient for TD-BOUND, strictly stronger, concrete. Unproved.
   582	This is the only statement on the list that could actually *be* a
   583	lemma implying the prize rather than renaming it.
   584	
   585	**KME-finite.** A type-wise bound with some
   586	\(C_{\alpha,\beta}<\infty\). Still new global geometry; Prop 3 shows
   587	it is not in the local laws even for type \((2,3)\). A universal
   588	absolute \(C\) independent of type would hit the iteration
   589	obstruction; Sol’s statement is per type, which is the right
   590	quantifier.
   591	
   592	**What an emission proof must import.** At least SP, because the
   593	one-pole sector has no merge to compare. SP does not follow from
   594	refining FC5. A proof of the full bound must control normalized
   595	mismatch energy at divergence centers (KME-2 / PCC or something that
   596	implies them). That information is not in \((w,M)\).
   597	
   598	No present FC5 consequence was missed that would prove SP, KME-2,
   599	KME-finite, or even a type-\((2,3)\) bound on \(A\) in Prop 3.
